---
source: tests/cli/help_snapshots_test.rs
expression: "help_output(&[subcommand, \"--help\"])"
---
Update topic fields such as title, notes, labels, markers, links, or images.

Usage: xmind set [OPTIONS] --node <NODE> <--dry-run|--apply> <WORKBOOK>

Arguments:
  <WORKBOOK>  Path to the .xmind workbook

Options:
      --node <NODE>                    Topic selector to update
      --title <TITLE>                  Replace the topic title
      --note <NOTE>                    Replace the topic note
      --append-note <APPEND_NOTE>      Append text to the topic note
      --set-labels <SET_LABELS>        Replace all labels with a comma-separated list
      --add-label <ADD_LABEL>          Add one label
      --remove-label <REMOVE_LABEL>    Remove one label
      --set-markers <SET_MARKERS>      Replace all markers with a comma-separated list
      --add-marker <ADD_MARKER>        Add one marker id
      --remove-marker <REMOVE_MARKER>  Remove one marker id
      --hyperlink <HYPERLINK>          Set the topic hyperlink
      --image <IMAGE>                  Attach an image from this path
      --image-alt <IMAGE_ALT>          Alt text for the attached image
      --image-title <IMAGE_TITLE>      Title text for the attached image
      --clear <FIELD>                  Clear a field such as note or hyperlink
      --dry-run                        Preview the change without writing the workbook
      --apply                          Write the change to the workbook
      --backup                         Create a safety backup before applying changes
      --json                           Emit a JSON command envelope
      --format <FORMAT>                Select the human or machine-readable output format [default: text] [possible values: text, json, compact-json, markdown, outline, assets]
      --fields <FIELDS>                Limit JSON output to comma-separated field paths
      --quiet                          Suppress non-essential text output
      --no-color                       Disable ANSI color in text output
      --sheet <SHEET>                  Select a sheet by title
      --sheet-id <SHEET_ID>            Select a sheet by stable id
      --sheet-index <SHEET_INDEX>      Select a sheet by zero-based index
  -h, --help                           Print help

Examples:
  xmind set roadmap.xmind --node path:/Launch --title "Launch plan" --dry-run
  xmind set roadmap.xmind --node path:/Launch --append-note "Owner: PM" --apply --backup
  xmind set roadmap.xmind --node path:/Launch --add-label priority --add-marker task-start --dry-run
